A||N||9||bcwawright||Still Lost! Where is the illusive Fan Switch?||||2||
Z||000000||bcwawright||05-20-2001||08:27 PM||||After 2 six pacs of Bud Lite I still can't find that Fan Switch....anyone want to come over for a beer and some barbuced ribs...maybe we can find it before we have to go to work monday.<BR>Any help in locating this rascal would be greatly appreciated,,,,,,,,,by the way I can't find my girl friend either but thats another story.<BR>Thanks in advance.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||2
Z||000001||Bob Englert||05-20-2001||08:33 PM||||You should be able to find it next to the EGR solenoid and just in front of the thermostat housing.  It has a single wire connection that is a sqeeze and pull type to release.<P>It might be easier to see if you remove the mounting screw that holds the EGR soleniod so you can move it out of the way a little.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||05-21-2001||10:41 AM||||bcwawright - I did get your email, and Bob Englert's description is better than I could have ever given.  Just start looking for wires in that general area and follow them until you find what they are attached to.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||bcwawright||05-21-2001||11:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>bcwawright - I did get your email, and Bob Englert's description is better than I could have ever given.  Just start looking for wires in that general area and follow them until you find what they are attached to.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the help<P>Bruce<BR>88GT<P>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Bruce||05-21-2001||11:35 AM||||Let me know how it goes; I tried to change the fan switch and could never get close to getting it out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bcwawright||05-21-2001||11:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bruce:<BR><B>Let me know how it goes; I tried to change the fan switch and could never get close to getting it out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi Bruce<BR>Just got the switch installed it was not hard to take out...the new one went in fine...I coated threads with a copper based anti-seize grease so if I ever need to remove again it will come out easier.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||RacinRob||05-21-2001||01:02 PM||||what color is the fan switch wire?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by RacinRob (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bruce||05-21-2001||01:09 PM||||Bruce (88 GT),<BR>How were you able to get around all the obstacles near the fan switch? Did you remove anything? I couldn't get my hand in position to detach the wires and unscrew the switch.<BR>Have you joined the "Anti-Bruce Defamation League?"<P>Bruce (86 GT)||||reg||1
Z||000008||bcwawright||05-21-2001||01:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bruce:<BR><B>Bruce (88 GT),<BR>How were you able to get around all the obstacles near the fan switch? Did you remove anything? I couldn't get my hand in position to detach the wires and unscrew the switch.<BR>Have you joined the "Anti-Bruce Defamation League?"<P>Hi Bruce<BR>No haven't joined that League yet..<BR>Someone wanted to know wire color..single green wire w/white stripe.<BR>I had the upper plenum off to paint....you are atleast going to have to remove the large vacuum line(I think it is for the brake system)and even with the plenum off that rascal was difficult to get my big hands down there to pinch both sides of the connector.<BR>Sorry I'm not much help.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT<P>Bruce (86 GT)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Two88GTs||05-21-2001||08:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RacinRob:<BR><B>what color is the fan switch wire?<P><BR>[This message has been edited by RacinRob (edited 05-21-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I used a 13/16" spark plug<BR>socket and a couple of 3/8" rachet extensions<BR>to get the fan switch out.  You need to remove the rubber hose that's clamped on to the upper intake plenum.  I used a long flathead screwdriver to pinch one side of the connector while using my index finger to unplug the switch.<P>------------------<BR>88GT 66k<BR>88GT 59k||||reg||1
